# Nothing is required here any more: the web container serves plain HTTP
# on the published port (WEB_PORT, default 8081) and expects an edge proxy
# (Traefik, nginx, ...) to terminate TLS, and the scores upstream is an
# internal compose-network address with a sensible default. The deploy
# loopback smoke test reads the port docker compose actually publishes,
# so a WEB_PORT override needs no second setting. Copy to .env only to
# override:
# SCORES_UPSTREAM=scores:8787
# WEB_PORT=8081
